  "summary": "This study primarily evaluates LiF/6 M HCl-etched Ti3C2Tx clay rolled into free-standing films. Three electrochemically compared Ti3C2Tx rolled-film electrodes differ by thickness: 5, 30, and 75 \u03bcm. The 5-\u03bcm film is the headline performer, reaching 900 F cm\u22123 and 245 F g\u22121 at 2 mV s\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4. The authors also fabricated a filtered Ti3C2Tx paper, a newly reported Ti2CTx paper, and activated-carbon counter electrodes, but did not report electrochemical capacitance for those materials in this paper; numerical capacitances for the 30- and 75-\u03bcm films are not printed in the supplied text."
}